+ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ Carvetto post-processor: Marlin 2.x (CNC / router use), millimetres
+ Written for Carvetto from scratch (clean-room). Licensed with Carvetto.
+ Dialect source: the Marlin G-code reference (marlinfw.org/docs/gcode/).
+
+ Firmware requirements
+ - SPINDLE_FEATURE (or LASER_FEATURE) for M3/M5. S is written in rpm, so
+   CUTTER_POWER_UNIT must be RPM; with PWM255 or PERCENT units the S value
+   must be scaled (edit SPINDLE_SPEED's multiplier). Some builds only offer
+   M3 (clockwise); this post never uses M4.
+ - ARC_SUPPORT (on by default) for G2/G3.
+ - !! An LCD controller, or EMERGENCY_PARSER (resume with M108), for the M0
+   tool-change pause. Without either, Marlin IGNORES M0 and the tool change
+   is skipped: the next toolpath runs with the previous tool.
+   (marlinfw.org/docs/gcode/M000-M001.html)
+ - INCH_MODE_SUPPORT for G21. Without it G21 is not recognised and Marlin
+   simply stays in millimetres, which is what this post wants.
+
+ Notes
+ - G21 selects millimetres, G90 absolute positioning. Marlin has no G94
+   (feed is always units per minute) and only accepts G17 when built with
+   CNC_WORKSPACE_PLANES, so neither is written; XY is Marlin's only arc
+   plane otherwise.
+ - Comments use ';' because Marlin only understands parenthesised comments
+   when built with PAREN_COMMENTS.
+ - Marlin runs G0 like G1 at the last feed rate, so rapids are slower than
+   on a dedicated CNC controller.
+ - No T word is written: on Marlin T selects an extruder.
+ - Tool change: stop the spindle, lift to safe Z, pause with M0 and a
+   message (resume from the LCD, or send M108 with EMERGENCY_PARSER; see the
+   firmware requirements above), lift to safe Z again in case Z was
+   re-zeroed, restart the spindle.
+ - G4 P is a dwell in MILLISECONDS on Marlin (G4 S would be seconds), so the
+   dwell seconds are multiplied by 1000.
+ - M30 is NOT written: on Marlin M30 deletes a file from the SD card. Marlin
+   has no program-end code; the program ends with the spindle off (M5) and
+   the tool parked at home XY above the work.
+ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

POST_NAME = "Marlin (mm) (*.gcode)"
FILE_EXTENSION = "gcode"
UNITS = "MM"
LINE_ENDING = "[10]"

+ Variables: VAR NAME = [tag|mode|prefix|format|multiplier]
VAR TOOL_NUMBER = [T|A||1.0]
VAR SPINDLE_SPEED = [S|A| S|1.0]
VAR FEED_RATE = [F|C| F|1.0]
VAR X_POSITION = [X|C| X|1.3]
VAR Y_POSITION = [Y|C| Y|1.3]
VAR Z_POSITION = [Z|C| Z|1.3]
VAR ARC_CENTRE_I = [I|A| I|1.3]
VAR ARC_CENTRE_J = [J|A| J|1.3]
VAR SAFE_Z = [SAFEZ|A| Z|1.3]
VAR HOME_X = [XH|A| X|1.3]
VAR HOME_Y = [YH|A| Y|1.3]
VAR DWELL_TIME = [DWELL|A| P|1.0|1000]

begin HEADER
"; [TP_FILENAME]"
"; Generated by [PRODUCT]"
"; Tool [T]: [TOOLNAME]"
"; [TOOLPATH_NAME]"
"G21"
"G90"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"M3[S]"
end

+ Each further toolpath with a different tool.
begin TOOLCHANGE
"M5"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"; Change to tool [T]: [TOOLNAME]"
"M0 Load tool [T] then resume"
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"; [TOOLPATH_NAME]"
end

begin SPINDLE_ON
"M3[S]"
end

+ A further toolpath with the same tool.
begin NEW_SEGMENT
"; [TOOLPATH_NAME]"
"M3[S]"
end

begin RAPID_MOVE
"G0[X][Y][Z]"
end

begin FEED_MOVE
"G1[X][Y][Z][F]"
end

begin PLUNGE_MOVE
"G1[X][Y][Z][F]"
end

begin RETRACT_MOVE
"G0[Z]"
end

begin CW_ARC_MOVE
"G2[X][Y][Z][I][J][F]"
end

begin CCW_ARC_MOVE
"G3[X][Y][Z][I][J][F]"
end

begin DWELL_MOVE
"G4[DWELL]"
end

begin FOOTER
"G0[SAFEZ]"
"M5"
"G0[XH][YH]"
"; End of program"
end
